# stow defaults its target to the PARENT of the stow dir. This repo is cloned to
# ~/dotfiles-public, whose parent is ~, which happens to be right — but pin it explicitly so it
# works regardless of clone location. --no-folding symlinks individual files rather than whole
# dirs, so a package owning ~/.tmux/ doesn't capture the entire directory.
--target=~
--no-folding
